+      "prompt": "Use case: precise-object-edit.\nEdit target: the supplied square three-panel forest / desert / winter race poster.\nPrimary request: in ALL THREE scenes the car must be STOPPED BEFORE the starting line, and the starting line must be a PROPER BLACK-AND-WHITE CHECKERBOARD BAND.\n\nCRITICAL CORRECTION: the current checkered stripes are BEHIND the rear wheels, so the cars have already crossed them. That is wrong. REMOVE those three old stripes completely, restoring the original road material beneath them. Then place ONE new correct checkerboard starting band per panel AHEAD OF THE CAR'S FRONT BUMPER in its direction of travel. The cars face AWAY from the viewer toward the upper-right background. AHEAD therefore means further up the road toward that background, never the foreground or below/behind the rear bumper. Each entire car, including front bumper and all four tyre contact points, is on the approach side of the line. There must be a clear strip of bare road between the nose and the nearest checkerboard edge, about half a metre in world space. No wheel, body, bumper or shadow should touch or overlap the band.\n\nKeep each rear-three-quarter car's design, ivory/navy livery, straight wheels and road-aligned heading. You may move the car slightly toward the foreground/left and modestly adjust its size, or extend the immediate straight, if needed to make the relationship unmistakable. Do not crop any part of a car. The three scenes must clearly read: viewer -> rear of waiting car -> front/nose -> short visible bare-road gap -> CHECKERED START LINE -> open track continuing forward. The road must remain straight through the car and starting band, bending only beyond the line. No part of any old starting stripe remains behind or under any car.\n\nCheckerboard construction: every starting band is a clean rectangular strip painted flat ACROSS the full road, with its long edge PERPENDICULAR to travel and parallel to the car's axles in world space. Use exactly THREE adjacent rows of evenly sized squares, roughly 12-16 columns across the road, all on ONE regular perspective grid. Adjacent cells alternate black/white in BOTH directions: row 1 BLACK WHITE BLACK WHITE; row 2 WHITE BLACK WHITE BLACK; row 3 BLACK WHITE BLACK WHITE. This is a real checkerboard with opposite colours in neighboring rows, NOT a single row of alternating rectangles, diagonal stripes, long bars, a zebra crossing, random triangles or checker-shaped shadows. The squares foreshorten consistently with the road plane. Keep the entire new band clearly readable ahead of each car.\n\nPreserve exactly three equal horizontal scenic panels and thin navy dividers, top pine forest / middle warm DESERT WITH COMPACTED SAND ROAD / bottom winter snowbanks and asphalt. Preserve the three-lens amber starter boards, existing scenery and mature matte cel-shaded 3D style, crisp controlled shadow bands and natural palette. No asphalt conversion of the desert, no road centre dashes, arrows, extra flags, text, numbers, logos, branding, smoke or motion effects. Stationary straight cars, one per panel, correctly waiting behind their lines. Square 1:1 output.",
